 "area": "retina",
 "description": "ls20 THE GAME IS COMMUNICATING (block 227000): the flash is a SIGN, not a fact with a built-in meaning. POSIT multiple candidate meanings (Posit Hypothesis nodes) from a GENERAL communicative vocabulary (sg_mint_posits); TEST by acting+residual (sg_want_test probe as-is -> sg_refute/sg_confirm, the 221/222 sd-loop applied to a sign); ACT on the confirmed meaning (sg_act_requirement -> transform_required -> sk_seek the only-other salient shape -> sk_pass). Controls: cycling (no interp), hardcode_reward (fixed wrong posit), no_test (posits but never tests). Guarded on game.seek_on==1 (default-OFF, byte-identical) + game.arm. Integer-native; no Rust; reuses shape_decode_loop (217) + onset (223) + quanta_navigation (220) + ls20_frustration (226) + the substrate's hypothesis mint/confirm/revise pattern.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "ls20_seek",
  "description": "The game is a communicative partner; its signs mean nothing until interpreted. The agent posits candidate meanings, tests them by acting, confirms the one whose prediction survives the residual, and acts on it \u2014 seek the only-other salient shape, apply, pass. The interpretation is discovered; every decision is a rule."
 },
